Error [E0102]: `Iter` has no method `get`
  --> {work}/main.jet:14:37
    |
 14 |         &rows.push(Row{ name: parts.get(0), count: missing })
    |                                     ^^^
 Why: `Iter` is a one-pass source; `get` needs a materialized list, so collection consumes the source and allocates the list
 Fix: Materialize it first with `.to_list()`; this consumes the source and allocates a list
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0102

Error [E0107]: Nothing named `missing` exists here
  --> {work}/main.jet:14:52
    |
 14 |         &rows.push(Row{ name: parts.get(0), count: missing })
    |                                                    ^^^^^^^
 Why: A name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: Declare it first: `missing :: ...`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0107

